# Move / Copy-to-Workspace Sheet

::summary
One sheet, two entry actions: the title swaps "Move to workspace" / "Copy to workspace" per the ⋯ menu item used (Move to Workspace vs Copy to Workspace). Destination picker lists the user's workspaces; the current workspace renders inert. Moving keeps the link working via a redirect; copying makes an independent duplicate.
::

::modal[name=move-copy title="Move to workspace" width=360 placement=centered dismissible=true]

:::row[icon=folder action=moveDocToWorkspace href=#]
Personal
Only you
:::

:::row[icon=folder state=inert href=#]
cloudsurf
Current workspace
:::

:::row[icon=folder action=moveDocToWorkspace href=#]
ashley-brady
2 members
:::

::

Top-right ✕ per dismiss canon. In copy mode the row action is `copyDocToWorkspace` — same sheet name, same rows, the entry action swaps the title and the verb.

At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the sheet goes edge-to-edge with 10px side insets and auto width; the wide placement declared on the block is unchanged.
